---
import Article from "../../../layouts/Article.astro";
import KeyTakeaway from "../../../components/KeyTakeaway.astro";
import InfoBox from "../../../components/InfoBox.astro";
import ComparisonTable from "../../../components/ComparisonTable.astro";
import GiftPick from "../../../components/GiftPick.astro";
---

<Article
  title="Wingspan Gift Ideas: 10 Gifts for Wingspan Lovers (2026)"
  description="Gifts for someone who loves Wingspan: 3D-printed food tokens, a puffin first-player token, nest bowls, inserts for Wingspan Pocket, and picks for expansion owners — sorted by who they suit."
  game="wingspan"
  gameTitle="Wingspan"
  category="Guide"
  publishDate="2026-10-09"
>
  <p>
    Buying for a Wingspan fan is easier than it looks. They already own the game
    they love, so the best gift isn't another box — it's something that makes
    every game of Wingspan nicer to play. Here are ten gifts we'd be happy to
    unwrap ourselves, from small stocking stuffers to the upgrade they'll touch
    on every single turn.
  </p>

  <KeyTakeaway answer="The best gift for a Wingspan fan upgrades the game they already play. 3D-printed food tokens are the upgrade they'll handle every turn; a puffin first-player token or nest bowls make a perfect small gift; and if they own an expansion or Wingspan Pocket, a piece made for that exact box shows you paid attention." />

  <InfoBox type="tip" title="Before you buy: check their shelf">
    Wingspan comes in more than one box. Look for the base game, any of its
    expansions, the new compact <a href="/games/wingspan-pocket/">Wingspan Pocket</a>,
    and the dragon-themed sibling Wyrmspan. Several gifts below only make sense
    for one of them, so a quick look at their games shelf saves a wrong guess.
  </InfoBox>

  <h2>Small gifts and stocking stuffers</h2>
  <p>
    These are low-cost, fit in a stocking, and still get used every game.
  </p>

  <GiftPick
    slug="wingspan-puffin-token"
    label="Best small gift"
    note="A little 3D-printed puffin that marks the first player. It replaces a cardboard chit with a bird, which is exactly the kind of detail Wingspan fans love."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="wingspan-bird-nest-bowls"
    note="Nest-shaped bowls for food and eggs. Practical in the middle of the table, and they look the part."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="wingspan-player-tray"
    note="Keeps each player's food, eggs and cards in one place. An easy one to buy in a set, one for each regular player."
  />

  <h2>The upgrade they'll use every turn</h2>
  <p>
    If you're only buying one thing, make it this. Players gain and spend food on
    almost every turn, so the food tokens are the part of the game they handle
    most.
  </p>

  <GiftPick
    slug="wingspan-food-tokens"
    label="Our top pick"
    note="3D-printed invertebrates, seeds, fish, fruit and rodents that replace the cardboard tokens. Easier to tell apart, nicer to pick up, and they won't wear out."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="wingspan-goal-tracker"
    note="A raised tracker for the round-end goals, so everyone can see the standings at a glance instead of leaning over the board."
  />

  <h2>For owners of an expansion</h2>
  <p>
    Expansions add their own components, and those are the ones that tend to stay
    as flimsy cardboard.
  </p>

  <GiftPick
    slug="wingspan-nectar-tokens"
    label="Only if they own Oceania"
    note="Two-colour 3D-printed nectar tokens for the Oceania expansion. A thoughtful gift precisely because it's so specific."
  />

  <p>
    If they don't own an expansion yet, that's a gift in itself. Our
    <a href="/games/wingspan/best-expansions/">guide to the best Wingspan expansions</a>
    explains what each one adds, so you can pick the one that suits how they play.
  </p>

  <h2>For Wingspan Pocket owners</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/games/wingspan-pocket/">Wingspan Pocket</a> is Stonemaier's compact
    2026 edition, and it ships with everything loose in the box. Both of these were
    designed for that box from scratch.
  </p>

  <GiftPick
    slug="wingspan-pocket-insert"
    note="An insert with an egg tray and card holder, sized to the Pocket box so components stay sorted in a bag and the lid closes flush."
  />
  <GiftPick
    slug="wingspan-pocket-insert-sleeved"
    label="If they sleeve their cards"
    note="A one-piece version measured around sleeved cards, with room for all 60 eggs. Sleevers will appreciate that you noticed."
  />

  <h2>For the fan who also plays Wyrmspan</h2>

  <GiftPick
    slug="wyrmspan-resource-tokens"
    note="Gold, meat and crystal tokens for Wyrmspan, Wingspan's dragon-themed sibling. The same kind of upgrade, for the other game on their shelf."
  />

  <h2>For the friend with a 3D printer</h2>

  <GiftPick
    slug="wingspan-goal-tracker-stl"
    note="The print files for our goal tracker, as an instant download. They print it in their favourite filament, and you don't have to worry about shipping times."
  />

  <h2>Which Wingspan gift fits?</h2>

  <ComparisonTable>
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left p-3 bg-bark/[0.02] font-heading font-semibold text-bark/70">If they…</th>
          <th class="text-left p-3 bg-bark/[0.02] font-heading font-semibold text-bark/70">Give them</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Play the base game often</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Food tokens</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Need a small or stocking gift</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Puffin first-player token or nest bowls</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Own the Oceania expansion</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Nectar tokens</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Bought Wingspan Pocket</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Wingspan Pocket insert (sleeved version if they sleeve)</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Own a 3D printer</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">Goal tracker STL file</td></tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5"><td class="p-3">Don't own an expansion yet</td><td class="p-3 font-semibold">An expansion (see our expansion guide)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </ComparisonTable>

  <InfoBox type="warning" title="Order a little earlier than usual">
    Everything here is printed to order in our workshop in Sweden and shipped
    from there. Check the delivery estimate on the Etsy listing before you order,
    and give yourself a few extra days in December.
  </InfoBox>

  <p>
    Shopping for more than one gamer? Our
    <a href="/gifts/">gift guide for board gamers</a> covers other games, handmade
    pieces and gifts for every budget.
  </p>
</Article>
